From: amd64-extree maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] clients/terminal: omit UTF-8 string terminator from key input

xkb_keysym_to_utf8() returns a byte count that includes the trailing NUL.
That NUL is not terminal input. Sending it after non-ASCII keypresses makes
terminal echo display ^@ and can confuse terminal applications. Add only the
UTF-8 payload length to the bytes written to the pty.

This is a local fix for the pinned Weston 16.0.0 source, based on the
xkbcommon API contract documented in xkbcommon.h. No upstream commit is known.

--- a/clients/terminal.c
+++ b/clients/terminal.c
@@ -2576 +2576 @@
-				len += ret;
+				len += ret > 0 ? ret - 1 : 0;
